diagnosis_text:
I verified end-to-end reachability between campuses and OSPF health on the alleged fault device (router16). Cross-campus pings are working from multiple sources: for example, Campus 1 host pc1 (10.5.0.1) reaches Campus 2 hosts pc12 (172.16.30.12) and pc5 (172.16.10.5) with 0% loss; dc_pc5 (10.5.0.5) reaches pc14 (172.16.30.14) with 0% loss; and pc3 (10.6.0.3) reaches pc7 (172.16.10.7) with 0% loss. This contradicts a blanket outage of Campus 2 from Campus 1.

On router16, OSPF is healthy: “show ip ospf neighbor” shows two fully adjacent neighbors (Full/DR on eth2 172.30.1.1 to 172.30.1.2 and Full/Backup on bond0 10.2.2.1 to 10.2.2.2) with normal dead timers. The OSPF route table contains the expected prefixes on both sides, including 10.5.0.0/24 and 10.6.0.0/24 via 172.30.1.2, and 172.16.10/20/30.0/24 via 10.2.2.2. Packets are therefore routed correctly between campuses.

Note: systemctl reports frr.service as inactive (dead), but FRR is demonstrably running and exchanging OSPF; in this environment FRR is not managed by systemd, so that status is not authoritative.

Root cause: No fault found; the reported outage is not present now.

Corrective fix: None required; do not restart router16. If users still report problems, please capture exact source/destination IPs and timestamps and check local host firewall/DNS. Consider adding monitoring to alert on router16 OSPF neighbor loss for early detection. 
=== END ===